course: dictionary
lesson: 14168
title: Modestly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Modestly» is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. When a person does something modestly, they do not brag or show off about it. «She smiled modestly when the class clapped for her science project.» She did well, but she did not make a fuss about it.
explain: The word can also mean a small amount. «Prices rose modestly this year, by just a few pence.» Here, modestly tells you the change was small and not big. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Modestly can also describe a simple way of living. «The family lives modestly in a small flat, with no expensive holidays.» It means they do not spend much money or have many fancy things. A «modestly priced» toy is one that does not cost a lot.
fact: Modestly comes from the word modest, which means not boastful or showy.
fact: «Modestly» can mean without bragging: «He answered modestly when they praised his goal.»
fact: «Modestly» can mean a small or fair amount: «Sales grew modestly last month.»
fact: «Modestly» can mean simply, not expensively: «They live modestly.»
fact: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
exercise: «She smiled modestly when everyone cheered for her.» What does modestly mean here? | Angrily, because she wanted more praise | Quickly, before the cheering stopped | *Without boasting about her success | Loudly and proudly, so everyone could see
exercise: «Prices rose modestly this year.» What does modestly mean here? | Unfairly, because of the shop owner | Sadly, after a long wait | Very quickly and by a huge amount | *By a small amount, not a lot
exercise: «They live modestly, with simple food and no expensive holidays.» What does modestly mean here? | *Simply, without spending much money | Noisily, with lots of visitors | In a grand house with many servants | Happily, after winning a prize
test: «He thanked the crowd modestly and walked off the stage.» Which word tells you he did not show off? | Crowd | *Modestly | Thanked | Stage
test: A shop sells modestly priced bikes. What does modestly priced mean? | Free to take home | *Not very expensive, a fair price | Very expensive, worth a fortune | Broken and old
exam: «The hero saved the village, but she only shrugged modestly and said, "Anyone would have helped." What does modestly mean? | Angrily, because nobody thanked her | Quickly, before anyone could ask questions | *Without bragging about her brave deed | Loudly, so the whole village could hear
